{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:03:23.461Z","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\.claude\\plans\\there-are-a-few-distributed-kettle.md","content":"# Plan: Unity-side TODOs in StratusFieldLink (publish path)\n\n## Context\n\nThe Unity project has three `TODO(candidate)` markers, all on the same seam:\n\n| Where | What is missing |\n|---|---|\n| `Runtime/Net/PublishService.cs:94` (`PublishRoutine`) | Every non-2xx is logged and reported as `RejectedByServer` with \"Publish failed.\" No distinction between offline, 4xx, 5xx, duplicate. |\n| `Runtime/Net/PublishService.cs:128` (`DrainQueue`) | Empty stub, nothing calls it. `PublishQueue` is written and tested but never filled or drained. |\n| `Tests/PlayMode/PublishFlowTests.cs:90` | No tests for offline / 400 / duplicate, because the behaviour does not exist. |\n\nGoal (README sections 1 and 2): a publish either lands, is rejected with a reason the foreman can read, or is saved and sent later, and the HUD says which.\n\nPaths below are relative to `unity/StratusFieldLink/Assets/StratusFieldLink/`.\n\n## Decisions (the \"decide\" part of the TODO)\n\n| Response | Outcome | Queue? | Foreman sees |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2xx | `Succeeded` | remove any queued copy | \"Published SK-…\" |\n| 409 (duplicate id) | `Succeeded` | remove | \"Already on the server\" |\n| Network error / timeout | `QueuedOffline` | enqueue + `Save()` | \"No signal. Saved, will send when back online\" |\n| 5xx, 408, 429 | retry in place up to `MaxAttempts` (3) with short backoff, then `QueuedOffline` | enqueue after last attempt | \"Server unavailable. Saved, will retry\" |\n| Other 4xx | `RejectedByServer` | never (a retry cannot succeed) | server's `error` text via `ApiErrorDto` |\n| Local validation | `FailedLocalValidation` (unchanged) | no | validation message |\n\nDuplicate is success because the realistic case is a timeout where the server did receive the sketch: the client queues it, retries, and must not treat \"already have it\" as a failure.\n\n## Steps\n\n### 1. `Runtime/Net/PublishService.cs`\n\n- **Pure classifier**: `public static PublishOutcome Classify(TransportResponse)` plus an `IsTransient` helper implementing the table. Static so it is EditMode-testable.\n- **Shared send coroutine**: `IEnumerator Send(FieldSketchDto, Action<PublishResult>)` holding the attempt loop (`WaitForSecondsRealtime(RetryDelaySeconds * attempt)`), used by both `PublishRoutine` and `DrainQueue`.\n- **Error body parsing**: `JsonUtility.FromJson<ApiErrorDto>` inside try/catch, falling back to \"Server rejected the sketch (status)\". The body may be empty or HTML.\n- **Snapshot before queueing**: clone via `JsonUtility` round-trip after stamping `clientLengthFeet`. Today the queued object would be the same reference as `SketchController.Current`, so later taps would mutate the queued sketch.\n- **Persist**: call `Queue.Save()` after every `Enqueue` / `Remove`; `PublishQueue` never saves itself.\n- **Re-entry guard**: `PublishRoutine` and `DrainQueue` return early if `IsBusy`.\n- **`DrainQueue`**: loop on `Queue.Peek()`:\n  - success or duplicate: remove, save, continue\n  - 4xx: remove, save, report, continue (avoids one bad sketch blocking the queue forever)\n  - network / transient: stop, leave the rest queued\n  - each item reports through the existing `PublishCompleted` event so the HUD needs no new wiring\n- **Drain triggers** (the \"something should call this\"):\n  - `Start()` when the queue loaded non-empty\n  - after any successful publish\n  - `OnApplicationPause(false)` / `OnApplicationFocus(true)`\n  - an `Update` timer every `DrainIntervalSeconds` (about 20s) while `Queue.Count > 0`\n  - `Application.internetReachability == NotReachable` used only as a cheap skip. It reports the interface, not real reachability, and is always reachable in the Editor, so it cannot be the trigger.\n- **Test seams**: make `Queue` settable; public `MaxAttempts`, `RetryDelaySeconds`, `DrainIntervalSeconds`, `AutoDrain`.\n\n### 2. `Runtime/UI/FieldHud.cs`\n\n- `OnPublishCompleted`: keep `result.Message`, prefix by outcome so the four cases are distinguishable at a glance.\n- On `Succeeded` or `QueuedOffline`, call `controller.StartNewSketch()`. The id is now handed off; editing and re-publishing it would be silently ignored by an idempotent server.\n\n### 3. Tests\n\n`Tests/PlayMode/PublishFlowTests.cs`. Change `SetUp` first: inject `new PublishQueue(TestKey)`, `RetryDelaySeconds = 0`, `AutoDrain = false`, delete the key in `TearDown`. The current `SetUp` uses the default PlayerPrefs key, which would start writing real prefs once `Save()` is wired.\n\nUse existing `StubFieldLinkTransport.Offline()`, `.Status()`, and `ScriptedResponses`:\n\n- offline: `QueuedOffline`, `Queue.Count == 1`, a fresh `PublishQueue(TestKey).Load()` still has it\n- 400 with `{\"error\":\"...\"}`: `RejectedByServer`, message contains server text, queue empty, `CallCount == 1`\n- 500, 500, 201: `Succeeded`, `CallCount == 3`\n- 500 x3: `QueuedOffline`, `CallCount == 3`\n- 409: `IsSuccess`\n- same sketch published twice offline: `Queue.Count == 1`\n- queued copy unchanged after adding a node to the original\n- drain: 2 queued + 201s empties queue; first response offline stops at `CallCount == 1`; 400 then 201 drops the first and sends the second\n- one HUD test via `SketchSceneFactory.Build()` with the stub injected: `Hud.RequestPublish()` offline, then assert `Hud.StatusLine` and a new `Controller.Current.id`\n\n`Tests/EditMode/PublishClassificationTests.cs` (new): table test over `Classify` (0/network, 200, 201, 400, 404, 408, 409, 429, 500, 503).\n\n### 4. Adjacent bug that blocks this path (not a TODO, recommend including)\n\n`Runtime/Geometry/SketchGeometry.cs:22` measures `dx`/`dz` only. A pure vertical drop is 0 ft, so `SketchValidation` rejects it as \"too short\" before the network is ever touched, and `clientLengthFeet` is light on any run with elevation change. This is README ticket #4. The server's `RunGeometry` is already 3D.\n\n- Add `dy` to the distance, fix the doc comment that rationalises it.\n- EditMode tests: 12 ft vertical drop measures 12 and validates; riser + horizontal sums correctly.\n- Existing geometry tests are all flat, so they stay green.\n\n## Dependency outside the Unity project\n\n`POST /api/sketches` does not exist yet (`src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/SketchEndpoints.cs:59`). The client plan assumes:\n\n- 201 on create\n- replay of an existing id returns 200 (or 409) and does not overwrite; `InMemorySketchRepository.Upsert` currently overwrites, which would reset status and history on a retry\n- 400 body `{ \"error\": \"...\", \"failures\": [...] }` so `ApiErrorDto` parses\n- a request DTO rather than binding `FieldSketch`, so a client cannot set `status` / `history`\n\nUnity work and tests do not need the endpoint (stub transport), but the manual end-to-end check does.\n\n## Order for a 60-minute box\n\n1. Geometry fix + tests (5 min, unblocks vertical publishes)\n2. `Classify` + `Send` + `PublishRoutine` + PlayMode tests\n3. `DrainQueue` + triggers + tests\n4. HUD messages\n5. Server endpoint, then end-to-end check\n\n## Verification\n\n- Unity Test Runner: EditMode and PlayMode all green (existing 4 publish tests must still pass unchanged apart from `SetUp`).\n- Manual, once the endpoint exists:\n  1. `dotnet run` in `src/StratusFieldLink.Api`, Play the scene, publish: HUD shows published, sketch appears in `GET /api/sketches`.\n  2. Stop the API, publish: HUD shows saved, \"Pending offline: 1\".\n  3. Stop and restart Play mode: pending count still 1.\n  4. Restart the API: within the drain interval, pending goes to 0 and the sketch appears once.\n  5. Sketch a vertical drop (F key between two clicks at the same spot): length is non-zero and it publishes.\n"}}
