{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:37:38.958Z","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\.claude\\plans\\we-are-in-an-replicated-falcon.md","content":"# Stratus Field Link — interview checklist\n\n## Context\n\n60-minute AI-collaboration interview. The brief (`README.md`) asks you to close the\npublish loop between a Unity field app, a .NET 8 API and a Vue dashboard, make it\nsurvive a bad network, add a throughput view, and fix a field bug. You are not\nexpected to finish everything: ship a coherent slice and say what you cut. The\nproctor notes process (design up front, verification, pushing back on AI) as much\nas outcome. This is a checklist to work from, ordered by suggested priority.\n\nNothing here has been run yet: I read the code but did not execute either test suite.\n\n## 0. Before the clock / housekeeping\n\n- [ ] Sign `PRIVACY_RELEASE.md` (name, date, signature, recording consent box)\n- [ ] Run `./start.sh` from repo root (records the terminal)\n- [ ] Confirm `dotnet test` is green and Unity opens (Stratus → Build Field Sketch Scene)\n- [ ] **Line-ending noise:** `git status` shows 74 modified files, but only 3 differ\n      once CR-at-EOL is ignored (`interview.log`, `Packages/manifest.json`,\n      `ProjectVersion.txt`). `core.autocrlf` is `false`. Decide how to handle this\n      before `end.sh` commits, or the diff will bury your real work.\n- [ ] `ProjectVersion.txt` changed: check your Unity version is still 2022.3 LTS\n\n## 1. Fix the bug (ticket) — smallest, best-defined, do first\n\nRoot cause: `unity/.../Runtime/Geometry/SketchGeometry.cs:22` `TotalLengthFeet`\nmeasures only `dx`/`dz` (plan length) and ignores `y`. The API's\n`src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Domain/RunGeometry.cs:12` is correctly 3D.\n\nBoth symptoms are the same bug:\n- Vertical drop → client length 0 → `SketchValidation.cs:69` says \"too short\"\n- Multi-level runs → `clientLengthFeet` comes in light (the dashboard \"Field said\"\n  column and `LengthMismatchCount`)\n\n- [ ] Add `dy` to `SketchGeometry.TotalLengthFeet`; fix the misleading doc comment\n- [ ] EditMode test: vertical riser `(0,10,0)→(0,22,0)` is 12 ft (mirror\n      `RunGeometryTests.TotalLengthFeet_VerticalRiser_CountsTheRise`)\n- [ ] EditMode test: a pure vertical drop passes `SketchValidation.Validate`\n- [ ] EditMode test: mixed run (horizontal + riser) sums in 3D\n- [ ] Worth saying out loud: the seed data (`scripts/generate-seed.mjs:175`) bakes in\n      plan-only client lengths, so historic mismatches stay. The server total\n      (`TotalPublishedFeet`) already uses the 3D number; confirm which figure the\n      shop was actually reading.\n- [ ] Note the duplicated logic (API + Unity) in `PROCESS.md` as a follow-up\n\n## 2. Close the publish loop — API\n\nFile: `src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/SketchEndpoints.cs:59`\n\n- [ ] Add `POST /api/sketches` with a dedicated request DTO in `Api/Dtos.cs`\n      (don't bind `FieldSketch` directly: a client could post `status`/`history`)\n- [ ] Match the Unity wire shape in `Runtime/Model/SketchDtos.cs`: `id`, `packageId`,\n      `crewId`, `discipline`, `diameterInches`, `material`, `nodes[{x,y,z}]`,\n      `capturedAtUtc` (ISO string), `clientLengthFeet`, `clientVersion`\n- [ ] Server sets `Status = Published`, `PublishedAtUtc = UtcNow`, and a history entry\n- [ ] Run `SketchValidator.Validate` → 400 with failures. The Unity side expects\n      an `{ \"error\": \"...\" }` body (`ApiErrorDto`), so keep that shape\n- [ ] Decide duplicate behaviour. Careful: `InMemorySketchRepository.Upsert`\n      overwrites, so a naive retry would reset an Approved sketch back to\n      Published. Suggested: check `repo.Find(id)` first; if present return 200 with\n      the existing record and don't overwrite (201 on first create)\n- [ ] xUnit tests: 201 on valid, 400 on invalid, duplicate is idempotent, new\n      sketch appears in `GET /api/sketches` and `/api/dashboard`. `Program` is\n      already `partial` for `WebApplicationFactory`; check the test csproj has\n      `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing`\n\n## 3. Close the publish loop + bad network — Unity\n\nFile: `unity/.../Runtime/Net/PublishService.cs:94`\n\nToday every non-2xx, including no signal, is reported as `RejectedByServer`.\n\n- [ ] No signal / timeout (`response.IsNetworkError`) → `Queue.Enqueue` + `Queue.Save()`\n      → `QueuedOffline`. (`Enqueue` does not save on its own.)\n- [ ] 4xx → `RejectedByServer`, parse `ApiErrorDto` and show the server's message;\n      do not queue\n- [ ] 5xx → bounded retry (e.g. a few attempts with backoff), then queue\n- [ ] Duplicate (200 from server) → treat as success\n- [ ] Implement `DrainQueue()` (`PublishService.cs:131`): peek, post, remove on\n      success or 4xx, stop on network error; and call it from somewhere (on\n      start, after a successful publish, or on a timer)\n- [ ] Foreman can tell what happened: distinct messages per outcome through\n      `PublishCompleted` → `FieldHud.OnPublishCompleted`; \"Pending offline\" count\n      is already drawn at `FieldHud.cs:106`\n- [ ] Gotcha: `FieldHud.RequestPublish` passes `controller.Current` by reference,\n      and nothing starts a new sketch after success, so pressing Publish twice\n      re-sends the same id, and a queued sketch can still be edited\n- [ ] Keep retry/outcome decision logic out of the MonoBehaviour where practical\n      (rubric item 7: Unity concerns out of testable logic)\n\n## 4. Unity tests for the publish path\n\n- [ ] PlayMode (`Tests/PlayMode/PublishFlowTests.cs:90`), using\n      `StubFieldLinkTransport.Offline()`, `.Status(...)`, and `ScriptedResponses`:\n  - [ ] offline → `QueuedOffline`, queue count 1\n  - [ ] 400 → `RejectedByServer`, message surfaced, not queued\n  - [ ] 5xx then 201 → succeeds after retry, call count as expected\n  - [ ] offline then `DrainQueue` with a 201 → queue empty\n  - [ ] same sketch twice → one queue entry / success on duplicate\n- [ ] EditMode: any pure decision logic you extract\n- [ ] Note: tests use the real `PlayerPrefs` key via `PublishQueue.DefaultStorageKey`\n\n## 5. Throughput (under-specified on purpose)\n\n- [ ] Pick a definition and write it down first. Suggested: per UTC day over the\n      last 14 days — sketches published, feet published, sketches reviewed\n      (Approved + Rejected, dated from `History`), plus backlog\n- [ ] Add endpoint at `DashboardEndpoints.cs:47` + DTO in `Dtos.cs`\n- [ ] Web: `fetchThroughput` in `src/stratus-field-link-web/src/lib/api.ts:24`, type\n      in `lib/types.ts`, replace the placeholder panel at `App.vue:63`\n- [ ] One xUnit test on the aggregation\n- [ ] Caveat for `PROCESS.md`: seed timestamps are rebased to \"now\"\n      (`SeedTimeRebaser`), and the existing \"awaiting review\" count only includes\n      `Published`, not `UnderReview`\n\nThis is the most cuttable item. An API-only version with the definition written\ndown is a reasonable slice.\n\n## 6. Deliverables / finishing\n\n- [ ] Fill in `PROCESS.md`: AI tools used; where AI was wrong (esp. Unity); how\n      you validated; throughput assumptions; offline/duplicate/server-error\n      decisions; what you cut and why; what's next\n- [ ] Update README run instructions only if you changed how anything starts\n- [ ] Final `dotnet test` + Unity EditMode and PlayMode runs\n- [ ] Exit the recording shell, run `./end.sh`\n- [ ] `git push origin HEAD` and share the URL\n\n## Suggested order for 60 minutes\n\n1 (bug + tests) → 2 (POST + tests) → 3 (Unity outcomes + queue) → 4 (PlayMode\ntests) → 5 (throughput, if time) → 6. Commit after each; commit cadence and\ntime-to-first-passing-test are recorded.\n\n## Verification\n\n- API: `dotnet test` from repo root; `dotnet run` in `src/StratusFieldLink.Api`,\n  then `curl -X POST http://localhost:5072/api/sketches` with a sample body, and\n  confirm it appears in `GET /api/sketches` and on `http://localhost:5173`\n- Unity: Test Runner → EditMode and PlayMode; then Play, sketch a riser with\n  R/F, publish with the API up, stop the API and publish again to see the\n  offline path and the pending count, restart and confirm the queue drains\n"}}
{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:37:39.198Z","tool_name":"ExitPlanMode","tool_input":{"plan":"# Stratus Field Link — interview checklist\n\n## Context\n\n60-minute AI-collaboration interview. The brief (`README.md`) asks you to close the\npublish loop between a Unity field app, a .NET 8 API and a Vue dashboard, make it\nsurvive a bad network, add a throughput view, and fix a field bug. You are not\nexpected to finish everything: ship a coherent slice and say what you cut. The\nproctor notes process (design up front, verification, pushing back on AI) as much\nas outcome. This is a checklist to work from, ordered by suggested priority.\n\nNothing here has been run yet: I read the code but did not execute either test suite.\n\n## 0. Before the clock / housekeeping\n\n- [ ] Sign `PRIVACY_RELEASE.md` (name, date, signature, recording consent box)\n- [ ] Run `./start.sh` from repo root (records the terminal)\n- [ ] Confirm `dotnet test` is green and Unity opens (Stratus → Build Field Sketch Scene)\n- [ ] **Line-ending noise:** `git status` shows 74 modified files, but only 3 differ\n      once CR-at-EOL is ignored (`interview.log`, `Packages/manifest.json`,\n      `ProjectVersion.txt`). `core.autocrlf` is `false`. Decide how to handle this\n      before `end.sh` commits, or the diff will bury your real work.\n- [ ] `ProjectVersion.txt` changed: check your Unity version is still 2022.3 LTS\n\n## 1. Fix the bug (ticket) — smallest, best-defined, do first\n\nRoot cause: `unity/.../Runtime/Geometry/SketchGeometry.cs:22` `TotalLengthFeet`\nmeasures only `dx`/`dz` (plan length) and ignores `y`. The API's\n`src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Domain/RunGeometry.cs:12` is correctly 3D.\n\nBoth symptoms are the same bug:\n- Vertical drop → client length 0 → `SketchValidation.cs:69` says \"too short\"\n- Multi-level runs → `clientLengthFeet` comes in light (the dashboard \"Field said\"\n  column and `LengthMismatchCount`)\n\n- [ ] Add `dy` to `SketchGeometry.TotalLengthFeet`; fix the misleading doc comment\n- [ ] EditMode test: vertical riser `(0,10,0)→(0,22,0)` is 12 ft (mirror\n      `RunGeometryTests.TotalLengthFeet_VerticalRiser_CountsTheRise`)\n- [ ] EditMode test: a pure vertical drop passes `SketchValidation.Validate`\n- [ ] EditMode test: mixed run (horizontal + riser) sums in 3D\n- [ ] Worth saying out loud: the seed data (`scripts/generate-seed.mjs:175`) bakes in\n      plan-only client lengths, so historic mismatches stay. The server total\n      (`TotalPublishedFeet`) already uses the 3D number; confirm which figure the\n      shop was actually reading.\n- [ ] Note the duplicated logic (API + Unity) in `PROCESS.md` as a follow-up\n\n## 2. Close the publish loop — API\n\nFile: `src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/SketchEndpoints.cs:59`\n\n- [ ] Add `POST /api/sketches` with a dedicated request DTO in `Api/Dtos.cs`\n      (don't bind `FieldSketch` directly: a client could post `status`/`history`)\n- [ ] Match the Unity wire shape in `Runtime/Model/SketchDtos.cs`: `id`, `packageId`,\n      `crewId`, `discipline`, `diameterInches`, `material`, `nodes[{x,y,z}]`,\n      `capturedAtUtc` (ISO string), `clientLengthFeet`, `clientVersion`\n- [ ] Server sets `Status = Published`, `PublishedAtUtc = UtcNow`, and a history entry\n- [ ] Run `SketchValidator.Validate` → 400 with failures. The Unity side expects\n      an `{ \"error\": \"...\" }` body (`ApiErrorDto`), so keep that shape\n- [ ] Decide duplicate behaviour. Careful: `InMemorySketchRepository.Upsert`\n      overwrites, so a naive retry would reset an Approved sketch back to\n      Published. Suggested: check `repo.Find(id)` first; if present return 200 with\n      the existing record and don't overwrite (201 on first create)\n- [ ] xUnit tests: 201 on valid, 400 on invalid, duplicate is idempotent, new\n      sketch appears in `GET /api/sketches` and `/api/dashboard`. `Program` is\n      already `partial` for `WebApplicationFactory`; check the test csproj has\n      `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing`\n\n## 3. Close the publish loop + bad network — Unity\n\nFile: `unity/.../Runtime/Net/PublishService.cs:94`\n\nToday every non-2xx, including no signal, is reported as `RejectedByServer`.\n\n- [ ] No signal / timeout (`response.IsNetworkError`) → `Queue.Enqueue` + `Queue.Save()`\n      → `QueuedOffline`. (`Enqueue` does not save on its own.)\n- [ ] 4xx → `RejectedByServer`, parse `ApiErrorDto` and show the server's message;\n      do not queue\n- [ ] 5xx → bounded retry (e.g. a few attempts with backoff), then queue\n- [ ] Duplicate (200 from server) → treat as success\n- [ ] Implement `DrainQueue()` (`PublishService.cs:131`): peek, post, remove on\n      success or 4xx, stop on network error; and call it from somewhere (on\n      start, after a successful publish, or on a timer)\n- [ ] Foreman can tell what happened: distinct messages per outcome through\n      `PublishCompleted` → `FieldHud.OnPublishCompleted`; \"Pending offline\" count\n      is already drawn at `FieldHud.cs:106`\n- [ ] Gotcha: `FieldHud.RequestPublish` passes `controller.Current` by reference,\n      and nothing starts a new sketch after success, so pressing Publish twice\n      re-sends the same id, and a queued sketch can still be edited\n- [ ] Keep retry/outcome decision logic out of the MonoBehaviour where practical\n      (rubric item 7: Unity concerns out of testable logic)\n\n## 4. Unity tests for the publish path\n\n- [ ] PlayMode (`Tests/PlayMode/PublishFlowTests.cs:90`), using\n      `StubFieldLinkTransport.Offline()`, `.Status(...)`, and `ScriptedResponses`:\n  - [ ] offline → `QueuedOffline`, queue count 1\n  - [ ] 400 → `RejectedByServer`, message surfaced, not queued\n  - [ ] 5xx then 201 → succeeds after retry, call count as expected\n  - [ ] offline then `DrainQueue` with a 201 → queue empty\n  - [ ] same sketch twice → one queue entry / success on duplicate\n- [ ] EditMode: any pure decision logic you extract\n- [ ] Note: tests use the real `PlayerPrefs` key via `PublishQueue.DefaultStorageKey`\n\n## 5. Throughput (under-specified on purpose)\n\n- [ ] Pick a definition and write it down first. Suggested: per UTC day over the\n      last 14 days — sketches published, feet published, sketches reviewed\n      (Approved + Rejected, dated from `History`), plus backlog\n- [ ] Add endpoint at `DashboardEndpoints.cs:47` + DTO in `Dtos.cs`\n- [ ] Web: `fetchThroughput` in `src/stratus-field-link-web/src/lib/api.ts:24`, type\n      in `lib/types.ts`, replace the placeholder panel at `App.vue:63`\n- [ ] One xUnit test on the aggregation\n- [ ] Caveat for `PROCESS.md`: seed timestamps are rebased to \"now\"\n      (`SeedTimeRebaser`), and the existing \"awaiting review\" count only includes\n      `Published`, not `UnderReview`\n\nThis is the most cuttable item. An API-only version with the definition written\ndown is a reasonable slice.\n\n## 6. Deliverables / finishing\n\n- [ ] Fill in `PROCESS.md`: AI tools used; where AI was wrong (esp. Unity); how\n      you validated; throughput assumptions; offline/duplicate/server-error\n      decisions; what you cut and why; what's next\n- [ ] Update README run instructions only if you changed how anything starts\n- [ ] Final `dotnet test` + Unity EditMode and PlayMode runs\n- [ ] Exit the recording shell, run `./end.sh`\n- [ ] `git push origin HEAD` and share the URL\n\n## Suggested order for 60 minutes\n\n1 (bug + tests) → 2 (POST + tests) → 3 (Unity outcomes + queue) → 4 (PlayMode\ntests) → 5 (throughput, if time) → 6. Commit after each; commit cadence and\ntime-to-first-passing-test are recorded.\n\n## Verification\n\n- API: `dotnet test` from repo root; `dotnet run` in `src/StratusFieldLink.Api`,\n  then `curl -X POST http://localhost:5072/api/sketches` with a sample body, and\n  confirm it appears in `GET /api/sketches` and on `http://localhost:5173`\n- Unity: Test Runner → EditMode and PlayMode; then Play, sketch a riser with\n  R/F, publish with the API up, stop the API and publish again to see the\n  offline path and the pending count, restart and confirm the queue drains\n","planFilePath":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\.claude\\plans\\we-are-in-an-replicated-falcon.md"}}
