{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:48:55.900Z","tool_name":"Grep","tool_input":{"pattern":"\"history\"","path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\Documents\\GitHub\\senior-full-stack-with-unity-ai-code-challenge\\src\\Data\\sketches.seed.json","output_mode":"content","-B":8,"-A":14,"head_limit":50}}
{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:49:19.195Z","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\.claude\\plans\\can-you-add-a-vast-iverson.md","content":"# Plan: `POST /api/sketches` (publish a field sketch)\n\n## Context\n\nThe Unity field client can sketch a run but has nowhere to send it: `PublishService` already POSTs\n`FieldSketchDto` JSON to `/api/sketches`, and the API has only a TODO there\n(`src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/SketchEndpoints.cs:59`). The TODO asks us to decide the contract,\nvalidation, status code and duplicate-id behaviour (the tablet retries when it regains signal),\nwire up the existing `SketchValidator`, and make accepted sketches visible in `GET /api/sketches`\nand the dashboard without a restart.\n\nScope is the API endpoint and its tests only. The Unity-side handling of the response\n(`PublishService` TODO, queue draining) and the measurement-bug ticket are separate tasks.\n\n## Decisions\n\n| Question | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| Request body | New `PublishSketchRequest` record matching the Unity `FieldSketchDto` field for field: `id, packageId, crewId, discipline, diameterInches, material, nodes[{x,y,z}], capturedAtUtc, clientLengthFeet, clientVersion`. We do **not** bind `FieldSketch` directly, so a client cannot post `status`, `history`, `reviewNotes` or `publishedAtUtc`. |\n| Server-owned fields | `Status = Published`, `PublishedAtUtc = UtcNow`, `History = [Draft -> Published, actor = crewId]` (same shape as the seed data). `CapturedAtUtc` falls back to now if omitted. |\n| New id | `201 Created`, `Location: /api/sketches/{id}`, body = `SketchDetailDto` (`ToDetail()`). |\n| Validation failure | `400` with `{ error: \"<joined messages>\", failures: [{ field, message }] }`. `error` keeps the existing `{ error }` convention that Unity's `ApiErrorDto` parses; `failures` carries the per-field detail from `SketchValidator`. |\n| Same id, same content (a retry) | `200 OK` with the stored sketch, nothing rewritten (`PublishedAtUtc` and history untouched). Still a 2xx, so the client's `IsSuccess` holds. |\n| Same id, existing sketch is `Rejected` | Treated as the rework republish from the lifecycle (`Rejected -> Published`): replace content, set `Published`, new `PublishedAtUtc`, append history. `200 OK`. |\n| Same id, different content, not `Rejected` | `409 Conflict` with `{ error }`. We never silently overwrite something the shop may be reviewing, and never silently drop a foreman's change. |\n\n\"Same content\" compares the client-supplied fields, including nodes in order. A retry resends the\nidentical JSON, so exact comparison is enough.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/Dtos.cs`\n- Add `PublishSketchRequest` (nullable strings / `List<SketchNode>?` / `DateTime? CapturedAtUtc`, so\n  missing fields reach the validator instead of failing model binding).\n- Add to `DtoMapper`: `ToFieldSketch(this PublishSketchRequest)` (trims `Id`, null-coalesces strings\n  and nodes) and a small `SameContentAs` comparison used for the retry check.\n\n### `src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/SketchEndpoints.cs`\nReplace the TODO block with `app.MapPost(\"/api/sketches\", (PublishSketchRequest request, ISketchRepository repo) => ...)`:\n1. Map to `FieldSketch`, run `SketchValidator.Validate`; invalid -> 400.\n2. `repo.Find(id)`:\n   - none -> stamp server fields, `repo.Upsert`; return 201 if `Upsert` returned true, else 200\n     (covers two retries racing each other).\n   - `Rejected` -> carry over existing history + `ReviewNotes`, append `Rejected -> Published`, `Upsert`, 200.\n   - same content -> 200 with the existing sketch.\n   - otherwise -> 409.\n\nNo repository changes: `ISketchRepository.Upsert` / `Find` and the singleton\n`InMemorySketchRepository` already give us \"visible without a restart\", since\n`GET /api/sketches` and `/api/dashboard` read `repo.All()` on every request.\n\n### `src/StratusFieldLink.Api.Tests/`\n- `StratusFieldLink.Api.Tests.csproj`: add `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing` 8.0.x (`Program` is\n  already exposed as a partial class for this).\n- New `PublishSketchEndpointTests.cs` using `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`:\n  - valid publish -> 201 + Location; then appears in `GET /api/sketches`, `GET /api/sketches/{id}`,\n    and `totalSketches` on `/api/dashboard` goes up by one\n  - body posted exactly as Unity's `JsonUtility` would write it (camelCase, ISO `capturedAtUtc`) binds\n  - same body twice -> 201 then 200, one stored sketch, `publishedAtUtc` unchanged\n  - same id, different nodes -> 409, stored sketch unchanged\n  - republish of a seeded `Rejected` sketch -> 200, status `Published`, history extended\n  - invalid (one node / unknown discipline / blank id) -> 400 with `error` and matching `failures[].field`\n  - posted `status: \"Approved\"` is ignored -> stored as `Published`\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `dotnet test` from the repo root: existing suites stay green, new endpoint tests pass.\n2. Manual: `dotnet run` in `src/StratusFieldLink.Api`, then\n   - `curl -i -X POST http://localhost:5072/api/sketches -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"id\":\"SK-MANUAL1\",\"packageId\":\"PKG-CHW-L02\",\"crewId\":\"CREW-01\",\"discipline\":\"Piping\",\"diameterInches\":4,\"material\":\"Carbon Steel\",\"nodes\":[{\"x\":0,\"y\":10,\"z\":0},{\"x\":24,\"y\":10,\"z\":0}],\"capturedAtUtc\":\"2026-10-13T17:00:00Z\",\"clientLengthFeet\":24,\"clientVersion\":\"field-1.4.2\"}'` -> 201\n   - repeat it -> 200; change a node -> 409; drop to one node -> 400\n   - `curl \"http://localhost:5072/api/sketches?crewId=CREW-01&limit=1\"` shows `SK-MANUAL1` first, and it is listed on the web dashboard (`npm run dev`) under awaiting review.\n"}}
