{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:49:20.495Z","tool_name":"ExitPlanMode","tool_input":{"plan":"# Plan: `POST /api/sketches` (publish a field sketch)\n\n## Context\n\nThe Unity field client can sketch a run but has nowhere to send it: `PublishService` already POSTs\n`FieldSketchDto` JSON to `/api/sketches`, and the API has only a TODO there\n(`src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/SketchEndpoints.cs:59`). The TODO asks us to decide the contract,\nvalidation, status code and duplicate-id behaviour (the tablet retries when it regains signal),\nwire up the existing `SketchValidator`, and make accepted sketches visible in `GET /api/sketches`\nand the dashboard without a restart.\n\nScope is the API endpoint and its tests only. The Unity-side handling of the response\n(`PublishService` TODO, queue draining) and the measurement-bug ticket are separate tasks.\n\n## Decisions\n\n| Question | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| Request body | New `PublishSketchRequest` record matching the Unity `FieldSketchDto` field for field: `id, packageId, crewId, discipline, diameterInches, material, nodes[{x,y,z}], capturedAtUtc, clientLengthFeet, clientVersion`. We do **not** bind `FieldSketch` directly, so a client cannot post `status`, `history`, `reviewNotes` or `publishedAtUtc`. |\n| Server-owned fields | `Status = Published`, `PublishedAtUtc = UtcNow`, `History = [Draft -> Published, actor = crewId]` (same shape as the seed data). `CapturedAtUtc` falls back to now if omitted. |\n| New id | `201 Created`, `Location: /api/sketches/{id}`, body = `SketchDetailDto` (`ToDetail()`). |\n| Validation failure | `400` with `{ error: \"<joined messages>\", failures: [{ field, message }] }`. `error` keeps the existing `{ error }` convention that Unity's `ApiErrorDto` parses; `failures` carries the per-field detail from `SketchValidator`. |\n| Same id, same content (a retry) | `200 OK` with the stored sketch, nothing rewritten (`PublishedAtUtc` and history untouched). Still a 2xx, so the client's `IsSuccess` holds. |\n| Same id, existing sketch is `Rejected` | Treated as the rework republish from the lifecycle (`Rejected -> Published`): replace content, set `Published`, new `PublishedAtUtc`, append history. `200 OK`. |\n| Same id, different content, not `Rejected` | `409 Conflict` with `{ error }`. We never silently overwrite something the shop may be reviewing, and never silently drop a foreman's change. |\n\n\"Same content\" compares the client-supplied fields, including nodes in order. A retry resends the\nidentical JSON, so exact comparison is enough.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/Dtos.cs`\n- Add `PublishSketchRequest` (nullable strings / `List<SketchNode>?` / `DateTime? CapturedAtUtc`, so\n  missing fields reach the validator instead of failing model binding).\n- Add to `DtoMapper`: `ToFieldSketch(this PublishSketchRequest)` (trims `Id`, null-coalesces strings\n  and nodes) and a small `SameContentAs` comparison used for the retry check.\n\n### `src/StratusFieldLink.Api/Api/SketchEndpoints.cs`\nReplace the TODO block with `app.MapPost(\"/api/sketches\", (PublishSketchRequest request, ISketchRepository repo) => ...)`:\n1. Map to `FieldSketch`, run `SketchValidator.Validate`; invalid -> 400.\n2. `repo.Find(id)`:\n   - none -> stamp server fields, `repo.Upsert`; return 201 if `Upsert` returned true, else 200\n     (covers two retries racing each other).\n   - `Rejected` -> carry over existing history + `ReviewNotes`, append `Rejected -> Published`, `Upsert`, 200.\n   - same content -> 200 with the existing sketch.\n   - otherwise -> 409.\n\nNo repository changes: `ISketchRepository.Upsert` / `Find` and the singleton\n`InMemorySketchRepository` already give us \"visible without a restart\", since\n`GET /api/sketches` and `/api/dashboard` read `repo.All()` on every request.\n\n### `src/StratusFieldLink.Api.Tests/`\n- `StratusFieldLink.Api.Tests.csproj`: add `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing` 8.0.x (`Program` is\n  already exposed as a partial class for this).\n- New `PublishSketchEndpointTests.cs` using `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`:\n  - valid publish -> 201 + Location; then appears in `GET /api/sketches`, `GET /api/sketches/{id}`,\n    and `totalSketches` on `/api/dashboard` goes up by one\n  - body posted exactly as Unity's `JsonUtility` would write it (camelCase, ISO `capturedAtUtc`) binds\n  - same body twice -> 201 then 200, one stored sketch, `publishedAtUtc` unchanged\n  - same id, different nodes -> 409, stored sketch unchanged\n  - republish of a seeded `Rejected` sketch -> 200, status `Published`, history extended\n  - invalid (one node / unknown discipline / blank id) -> 400 with `error` and matching `failures[].field`\n  - posted `status: \"Approved\"` is ignored -> stored as `Published`\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `dotnet test` from the repo root: existing suites stay green, new endpoint tests pass.\n2. Manual: `dotnet run` in `src/StratusFieldLink.Api`, then\n   - `curl -i -X POST http://localhost:5072/api/sketches -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"id\":\"SK-MANUAL1\",\"packageId\":\"PKG-CHW-L02\",\"crewId\":\"CREW-01\",\"discipline\":\"Piping\",\"diameterInches\":4,\"material\":\"Carbon Steel\",\"nodes\":[{\"x\":0,\"y\":10,\"z\":0},{\"x\":24,\"y\":10,\"z\":0}],\"capturedAtUtc\":\"2026-10-13T17:00:00Z\",\"clientLengthFeet\":24,\"clientVersion\":\"field-1.4.2\"}'` -> 201\n   - repeat it -> 200; change a node -> 409; drop to one node -> 400\n   - `curl \"http://localhost:5072/api/sketches?crewId=CREW-01&limit=1\"` shows `SK-MANUAL1` first, and it is listed on the web dashboard (`npm run dev`) under awaiting review.\n","planFilePath":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\.claude\\plans\\can-you-add-a-vast-iverson.md"}}
{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:55:57.827Z","tool_name":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\Documents\\GitHub\\senior-full-stack-with-unity-ai-code-challenge\\src\\StratusFieldLink.Api\\Api\\Dtos.cs","old_string":"public sealed record StationCountDto(string Key, int Count);","new_string":"/// <summary>\n/// What the Unity field client sends on publish; mirrors its FieldSketchDto.\n/// Status, history and review notes are deliberately absent: the server owns those.\n/// </summary>\npublic sealed record PublishSketchRequest(\n    string? Id,\n    string? PackageId,\n    string? CrewId,\n    string? Discipline,\n    double DiameterInches,\n    string? Material,\n    List<SketchNode>? Nodes,\n    DateTime? CapturedAtUtc,\n    double ClientLengthFeet,\n    string? ClientVersion);\n\npublic sealed record StationCountDto(string Key, int Count);","replace_all":false}}
{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:56:40.761Z","tool_name":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\Documents\\GitHub\\senior-full-stack-with-unity-ai-code-challenge\\src\\StratusFieldLink.Api\\Api\\Dtos.cs","old_string":"    public static SketchDetailDto ToDetail(this FieldSketch s)\n        => new(s.ToSummary(), s.Nodes, s.History, s.ReviewNotes);","new_string":"    public static SketchDetailDto ToDetail(this FieldSketch s)\n        => new(s.ToSummary(), s.Nodes, s.History, s.ReviewNotes);\n\n    public static FieldSketch ToFieldSketch(this PublishSketchRequest r)\n        => new()\n        {\n            Id = (r.Id ?? \"\").Trim(),\n            PackageId = (r.PackageId ?? \"\").Trim(),\n            CrewId = (r.CrewId ?? \"\").Trim(),\n            Discipline = (r.Discipline ?? \"\").Trim(),\n            DiameterInches = r.DiameterInches,\n            Material = (r.Material ?? \"\").Trim(),\n            Nodes = r.Nodes?.Where(n => n is not null).ToList() ?? new List<SketchNode>(),\n            CapturedAtUtc = r.CapturedAtUtc ?? DateTime.UtcNow,\n            ClientLengthFeet = r.ClientLengthFeet,\n            ClientVersion = r.ClientVersion ?? \"\"\n        };\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// True when two publishes describe the same run. Compares what the foreman drew,\n    /// not the stamps the client re-applies on every attempt (clientVersion,\n    /// clientLengthFeet), so a retry after an app update still counts as a retry.\n    /// </summary>\n    public static bool SameContentAs(this FieldSketch a, FieldSketch b)\n        => string.Equals(a.PackageId, b.PackageId, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n           && string.Equals(a.CrewId, b.CrewId, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n           && a.Discipline == b.Discipline\n           && a.DiameterInches.Equals(b.DiameterInches)\n           && a.Material == b.Material\n           && a.Nodes.Count == b.Nodes.Count\n           && a.Nodes.Zip(b.Nodes).All(p =>\n               p.First.X.Equals(p.Second.X) && p.First.Y.Equals(p.Second.Y) && p.First.Z.Equals(p.Second.Z));","replace_all":false}}
{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:56:40.873Z","tool_name":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\Documents\\GitHub\\senior-full-stack-with-unity-ai-code-challenge\\src\\StratusFieldLink.Api\\Api\\SketchEndpoints.cs","old_string":"        // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n        // TODO(candidate): the Unity field client needs to publish a sketch here.\n        //\n        //   POST /api/sketches\n        //\n        // Decide the contract, the validation, the status code, and what happens\n        // when the same client-generated id is published twice (the field app\n        // retries when it comes back into signal). SketchValidator is already\n        // written and tested; wire it up.\n        //\n        // Whatever you accept has to show up in GET /api/sketches and on the\n        // dashboard without a restart.\n        // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n","new_string":"        // Publish from the Unity field client. The id is client-generated, so the\n        // tablet can retry safely when it comes back into signal:\n        //   new id                          -> 201\n        //   same id, same run (a retry)     -> 200, nothing rewritten\n        //   same id, currently Rejected     -> 200, republished after rework\n        //   same id, different run          -> 409\n        //   fails SketchValidator           -> 400\n        app.MapPost(\"/api/sketches\", (PublishSketchRequest request, ISketchRepository repo) =>\n        {\n            var sketch = request.ToFieldSketch();\n\n            var validation = SketchValidator.Validate(sketch);\n            if (!validation.IsValid)\n            {\n                return Results.BadRequest(new\n                {\n                    error = string.Join(\" \", validation.Failures.Select(f => f.Message)),\n                    failures = validation.Failures\n                });\n            }\n\n            var now = DateTime.UtcNow;\n            sketch.Status = SketchStatus.Published;\n            sketch.PublishedAtUtc = now;\n\n            var existing = repo.Find(sketch.Id);\n\n            if (existing is null)\n            {\n                sketch.History.Add(new StatusChange\n                {\n                    From = SketchStatus.Draft,\n                    To = SketchStatus.Published,\n                    AtUtc = now,\n                    Actor = sketch.CrewId\n                });\n\n                // Upsert returns false if a concurrent retry of the same publish won the race.\n                return repo.Upsert(sketch)\n                    ? Results.Created($\"/api/sketches/{Uri.EscapeDataString(sketch.Id)}\", sketch.ToDetail())\n                    : Results.Ok(sketch.ToDetail());\n            }\n\n            if (existing.Status == SketchStatus.Rejected)\n            {\n                sketch.Id = existing.Id;\n                sketch.ReviewNotes = existing.ReviewNotes;\n                sketch.History.AddRange(existing.History);\n                sketch.History.Add(new StatusChange\n                {\n                    From = SketchStatus.Rejected,\n                    To = SketchStatus.Published,\n                    AtUtc = now,\n                    Actor = sketch.CrewId\n                });\n\n                repo.Upsert(sketch);\n                return Results.Ok(sketch.ToDetail());\n            }\n\n            if (existing.SameContentAs(sketch))\n            {\n                return Results.Ok(existing.ToDetail());\n            }\n\n            return Results.Conflict(new\n            {\n                error = $\"Sketch '{existing.Id}' was already published with different content and is {existing.Status}.\"\n            });\n        });\n","replace_all":false}}
