{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:25:54.082Z","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\ambid\\.claude\\plans\\can-we-make-a-hashed-peacock.md","content":"# Plan: finish the publish seam in `PublishService`\n\n## Context\n\n`PublishService.PublishRoutine` treats every non-2xx the same: log it, report `RejectedByServer` with \"Publish failed.\", and drop the sketch. `PublishQueue` is written, tested and loaded in `Awake`, but nothing enqueues to it or drains it (`DrainQueue` is an empty stub). The README brief (parts 1 and 2) asks for sane handling of no-signal / 4xx / 5xx / duplicate id, and for the foreman to be able to tell which happened.\n\nThe server side is already in the working tree (`SketchEndpoints.cs`): `201` new, `200` same id + same content (safe retry), `409` same id + different content, `400` validation failure with `{ error, failures }`. Because the id is client-generated and the POST is idempotent, the client can resend freely.\n\n## Response handling\n\nOne classifier, used by both publish and drain:\n\n| Response | Class | Action | Outcome / message to foreman |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `201` | success | remove from queue if present | `Succeeded` – \"Published SK-…\" |\n| `200` | success (duplicate) | remove from queue if present | `Succeeded` – \"SK-… was already published.\" |\n| network error / timeout | offline | enqueue + `Save()` immediately, no inline retry (a 10s timeout x3 in a basement is just a frozen HUD) | `QueuedOffline` – \"No signal. Saved; will send when back online.\" |\n| `5xx`, `408`, `429` | transient | retry inline up to 3 attempts with backoff (1s, 2s); if still failing, enqueue + `Save()` | `QueuedOffline` – \"Server unavailable (503). Saved; will retry.\" |\n| `400` | permanent | never queue, never retry; parse body with the existing `ApiErrorDto` | `RejectedByServer` – server's `error` text |\n| `409` | permanent | never queue, never retry | `RejectedByServer` – \"SK-… was already published with different content. Start a new sketch.\" |\n| other `4xx` | permanent | never queue, never retry | `RejectedByServer` – \"Server refused the sketch (4xx).\" |\n\nNo new `PublishOutcome` values are needed; `StatusCode` + `Message` distinguish the cases.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. `unity/.../Runtime/Net/PublishService.cs` (main change)\n\n- Add tunables as public properties so tests can zero them: `MaxAttempts = 3`, `RetryDelaySeconds = 1f` (doubles per attempt), `AutoDrain = true`, `DrainIntervalSeconds = 15f`.\n- Extract `private IEnumerator SendRoutine(FieldSketchDto sketch, Action<PublishResult> onDone)`:\n  stamps `clientLengthFeet` / `clientVersion`, serialises, runs the attempt loop (`WaitForSecondsRealtime` between transient retries), classifies per the table and returns a `PublishResult`. It does **not** touch `IsBusy` or the queue, so publish and drain can share it.\n- `PublishRoutine`: validate locally (unchanged) -> `SendRoutine` -> apply the queue action:\n  - offline / transient-exhausted: enqueue a **copy** of the sketch (`JsonUtility` round-trip) then `Queue.Save()`. The copy matters: `controller.Current` stays editable after publish, and resending an edited sketch under an id that may already have landed would turn a safe retry into a `409`.\n  - success: `Queue.Remove(id)` + `Save()` if it was pending, then kick a drain (signal is evidently back).\n- Implement `DrainQueue()`:\n  - no-op if `IsBusy` or queue empty; sets `IsBusy` for the whole drain so the HUD's existing `IsBusy` guard keeps a manual publish from interleaving.\n  - loop on `Queue.Peek()`: success -> `Remove` + `Save`, continue; permanent rejection -> `Remove` + `Save`, raise `PublishCompleted` with the rejection so the foreman sees it, continue (otherwise one bad sketch blocks the queue forever); offline/transient -> stop, leave it and everything behind it queued.\n  - finish with one summary result (\"Sent N queued sketches.\" / \"Still offline, N pending.\").\n- Triggers for the drain: `Start()` (pending work from a previous session), after any successful publish, and a timer in `Update()` while `AutoDrain && Queue.Count > 0 && !IsBusy`. The interval doubles after a failed drain up to a 5 min cap and resets on success: \"retry, but not forever\" for inline attempts, sparse-but-never-lossy for queued work. `Application.internetReachability == NotReachable` is used only as a cheap skip; it reports adapter state, not whether Stratus is reachable, so the real test is the request itself.\n- Split `Complete` so per-item drain notifications don't clear `IsBusy` mid-drain.\n- Replace the `TODO(candidate)` blocks with a short comment describing the policy.\n\n### 2. `unity/.../Runtime/UI/FieldHud.cs` (small)\n\nAlready shows `result.Message` and \"Pending offline: N\", so the new messages surface with no structural change. Only tweak: don't overwrite the status line with \"Publishing…\" semantics for drain results — nothing needed beyond confirming it reads well in Play mode.\n\n### 3. `unity/.../Tests/PlayMode/PublishFlowTests.cs`\n\n`SetUp`: `RetryDelaySeconds = 0`, `AutoDrain = false`. `TearDown`: `PlayerPrefs.DeleteKey(PublishQueue.DefaultStorageKey)` (the service uses the real key). Uses the existing `StubFieldLinkTransport.ScriptedResponses`, `Offline()`, `Status()`. Replace the TODO with:\n\n- offline -> `QueuedOffline`, `Queue.Count == 1`, 1 call\n- queued copy is a snapshot (mutating the original after publish doesn't change the queued one)\n- `400` -> `RejectedByServer`, message is the server's `error`, not queued, 1 call\n- `409` -> `RejectedByServer`, not queued, 1 call\n- `200` (duplicate) -> `Succeeded`\n- `503` then `201` -> `Succeeded`, 2 calls, not queued\n- `503` x3 -> `QueuedOffline`, exactly `MaxAttempts` calls\n- drain: two queued, server accepts -> queue empty, persisted queue empty after `Load()`\n- drain: first response offline -> stops after 1 call, both still queued\n- drain: `400` on first, `201` on second -> both removed, rejection was raised via `PublishCompleted`\n\nNo changes to `PublishQueue`, `IFieldLinkTransport`, `UnityWebRequestTransport` or the API.\n\n## Deliberately not included (worth a line in PROCESS.md)\n\n- A sketch rejected during a drain is removed from the queue and reported, not kept in a dead-letter list for rework.\n- No per-item attempt cap in the queue; that would need a wrapper around the wire DTO and a storage format change.\n- HUD does not auto-start a new sketch after a successful publish, so editing and republishing the same id yields the `409` message.\n- Server note, not touched here: the endpoint comment promises \"same id, currently Rejected -> 200, republished after rework\", but the code returns `409` for any differing content.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Unity Test Runner: run **EditMode** (queue tests still green) and **PlayMode** (`PublishFlowTests` new cases).\n2. `dotnet test` from repo root to confirm the API side is untouched and green.\n3. Manual, end to end:\n   - API stopped -> sketch 2+ nodes -> Publish -> HUD shows \"No signal. Saved…\" and \"Pending offline: 1\".\n   - Stop Play, press Play again -> pending count still 1 (persisted).\n   - `dotnet run` the API -> within the drain interval the HUD reports the sketch sent, pending 0, and `curl http://localhost:5072/api/sketches?crewId=CREW-04` lists it.\n   - Publish the same sketch again -> \"already published\"; add a node and publish -> the `409` message.\n"}}
